<title>USA: Rally's seeks to amend underlying indenture.</title>
<headline>Rally's seeks to amend underlying indenture.</headline>
<dateline>LOUISVILLE, Ky. 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rally's Hamburgers Inc said Thursday it had begun soliciting consents from the holders of its 9-7/8 percent senior notes due 2000 to amend the underlying indenture.</p>
<p>This amendment would allow two of the company's stockholders, CKE Restaurants Inc and Fidelity National Financial Inc to acquire 35 percent or more of the outstanding shares of the company's common stock, without triggering the indenture's &quot;change of control&quot; provisions requiring the company to offer to purchase the senior notes at 101 percent of their face value.</p>
</text>
